#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid ""
"Do not include private keys, raw passwords, bearer secrets, subscription "
"URLs, or reusable authentication tokens in public reports."
msgstr ""
"公开报告中不要包含私钥、原始密码、bearer secret、订阅 URL 或可复用认证令牌。"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "Stop Conditions"
msgstr "停止条件"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid ""
"Stop expanding the search when you have identified the first failing "
"boundary and can reproduce it independently."
msgstr "当已经识别第一处失败边界并能独立复现时，就停止继续扩大排查范围。"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "listener does not bind → fix listener/build/config first;"
msgstr "listener 无法 bind → 先修复 listener/build/config；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "rule selects wrong outbound → fix DNS/rule/group state first;"
msgstr "规则选择错误 outbound → 先修复 DNS/rule/group 状态；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "TLS certificate fails → fix TLS trust/SNI first;"
msgstr "TLS 证书失败 → 先修复 TLS trust/SNI；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "gRPC returns status 12 → fix transport method/path/content type first;"
msgstr "gRPC 返回 status 12 → 先修复 transport method/path/content type；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid ""
"proxy auth succeeds but target connect fails → fix server routing/target "
"first;"
msgstr "代理认证成功但目标连接失败 → 先修复 server routing/target；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "only service mode fails → fix IPC/privilege/core lifecycle first."
msgstr "只有 service mode 失败 → 先修复 IPC/权限/core 生命周期。"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid ""
"Changing downstream layers before the upstream failure is resolved makes the "
"incident harder to reason about and can erase useful evidence."
msgstr "在上游失败尚未解决前修改下游层，会让故障更难推理，并可能抹掉有用证据。"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid ""
"The concrete observation/error paths used in this guide were checked against:"
msgstr "本指南使用的具体观测/错误路径已对照以下源码检查："

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid ""
"`Chimera_Client/clash-lib/src/app/api/runner.rs` and `app/api/handlers`;"
msgstr ""
"`Chimera_Client/clash-lib/src/app/api/runner.rs` 与 `app/api/handlers`；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "`Chimera_Client/clash-lib/src/app/dispatcher/dispatcher_impl.rs`;"
msgstr "`Chimera_Client/clash-lib/src/app/dispatcher/dispatcher_impl.rs`；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid ""
"`Chimera_Client/clash-lib/src/app/inbound` and `app/outbound/manager.rs`;"
msgstr ""
"`Chimera_Client/clash-lib/src/app/inbound` 与 `app/outbound/manager.rs`；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "`Chimera_Client/clash-lib/src/app/dns`;"
msgstr "`Chimera_Client/clash-lib/src/app/dns`；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "`Chimera_Client/clash-lib/src/proxy`;"
msgstr "`Chimera_Client/clash-lib/src/proxy`；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "`Chimera_Server/chimera_server_app/src/main.rs`;"
msgstr "`Chimera_Server/chimera_server_app/src/main.rs`；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "`Chimera_Server/chimera_server_lib/src/beginning`;"
msgstr "`Chimera_Server/chimera_server_lib/src/beginning`；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "`Chimera_Server/chimera_server_lib/src/handler`;"
msgstr "`Chimera_Server/chimera_server_lib/src/handler`；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid "`Chimera_Server/chimera_server_lib/src/reality`;"
msgstr "`Chimera_Server/chimera_server_lib/src/reality`；"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid ""
"the cross-project and external E2E tests catalogued in [Test Evidence and "
"Interoperability Matrix](./test-evidence.md)."
msgstr ""
"以及 [测试证据与互操作矩阵](./test-evidence.md) 中整理的跨项目与外部 E2E 测"
"试。"

#: src/troubleshooting.md
msgid ""
"This page should be updated when a failure boundary, controller endpoint, "
"feature gate, or test path changes in source."
msgstr ""
"当源码中的失败边界、controller endpoint、feature gate 或测试路径变化时，应同"
"步更新本页。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"This page describes the security boundaries that matter when deploying the "
"Chimera ecosystem. It is not a claim that one configuration is universally "
"secure; it is a checklist for understanding **which component trusts whom, "
"which secrets cross which boundary, and what an attacker can reach if one "
"layer is exposed**."
msgstr ""
"本页描述部署 Chimera 生态时真正重要的安全边界。它并不声称某一种配置在所有场景"
"都绝对安全，而是一份用于理解**哪个组件信任谁、哪些秘密跨越哪些边界，以及某一"
"层暴露后攻击者能够触达什么**的检查清单。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Protocol cryptography is only one part of the system. A correctly encrypted "
"VLESS/REALITY or Shadowsocks connection can still be undermined by an "
"unauthenticated LAN listener, leaked controller secret, unsafe fallback "
"target, DNS/TUN leak, over-privileged service, or logs containing reusable "
"credentials."
msgstr ""
"协议密码学只是整个系统的一部分。即使 VLESS/REALITY 或 Shadowsocks 连接本身正"
"确加密，也仍可能被未认证的 LAN listener、泄漏的 controller secret、不安全的 "
"fallback 目标、DNS/TUN 泄漏、权限过高的 service 或包含可复用凭据的日志破坏。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Use this page together with [End-to-End Troubleshooting](./"
"troubleshooting.md), [Implementation Status and Source Evidence](./"
"implementation-status.md), and the protocol-specific security sections."
msgstr ""
"请结合 [端到端故障排查](./troubleshooting.md)、[实现状态与源码证据](./"
"implementation-status.md) 以及各协议的安全章节阅读本页。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Trust Boundaries"
msgstr "信任边界"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "A typical desktop deployment crosses these boundaries:"
msgstr "典型桌面部署会跨越以下边界："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Service mode inserts another privileged boundary:"
msgstr "Service mode 会额外插入一个特权边界："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Android inserts a VPN boundary:"
msgstr "Android 则会插入一个 VPN 边界："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Each arrow can have a different attacker and different authentication model. "
"Do not treat “the proxy connection is encrypted” as protection for every "
"arrow."
msgstr ""
"每一条箭头都可能面对不同攻击者和不同认证模型。不要把“代理连接已加密”误认为所"
"有边界都因此得到保护。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Assets to Protect"
msgstr "需要保护的资产"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Treat these as security-sensitive assets:"
msgstr "应把以下内容视为安全敏感资产："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Shadowsocks passwords/PSKs and AEAD-2022 raw keys;"
msgstr "Shadowsocks 密码/PSK 与 AEAD-2022 原始密钥；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "AnyTLS passwords;"
msgstr "AnyTLS 密码；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Trojan passwords;"
msgstr "Trojan 密码；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "VLESS/VMess user identifiers where they grant service access;"
msgstr "能够授予服务访问权限的 VLESS/VMess 用户标识；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "REALITY private keys, client public-key configuration, and short IDs;"
msgstr "REALITY 私钥、客户端公钥配置和 short ID；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Hysteria 2 credentials;"
msgstr "Hysteria 2 凭据；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "TUIC UUID/password material;"
msgstr "TUIC UUID/密码材料；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "TLS private keys and client certificates;"
msgstr "TLS 私钥与客户端证书；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Chimera controller/API bearer secrets;"
msgstr "Chimera controller/API bearer secret；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "subscription URLs containing access tokens;"
msgstr "包含访问 token 的订阅 URL；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "generated runtime configuration when it contains credentials;"
msgstr "包含凭据时的生成运行时配置；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "service IPC/control capability;"
msgstr "service IPC/控制能力；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "DNS/routing policy when it reveals or controls user traffic."
msgstr "能够暴露或控制用户流量的 DNS/routing 策略。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"A value does not need to be a conventional password to be reusable "
"authentication material."
msgstr "一个值不必是传统意义上的密码，也可能属于可复用认证材料。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Threat Actors"
msgstr "威胁主体"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Useful threat categories include:"
msgstr "有用的威胁类别包括："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Actor"
msgstr "主体"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Typical capability"
msgstr "典型能力"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Local unprivileged user/process"
msgstr "本地非特权用户/进程"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Connect to local listeners/APIs, read world-readable files, influence local "
"DNS or environment."
msgstr "连接本地 listener/API、读取全局可读文件、影响本地 DNS 或运行环境。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "LAN peer"
msgstr "LAN 对端"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Reach listeners accidentally bound to LAN, probe unauthenticated SOCKS/HTTP/"
"Dokodemo endpoints."
msgstr ""
"访问意外绑定到 LAN 的 listener，探测未认证 SOCKS/HTTP/Dokodemo endpoint。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "On-path network observer"
msgstr "链路中间观察者"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"See IPs, ports, timing, sizes, plaintext protocols without TLS, and possibly "
"HTTP metadata."
msgstr ""
"观察 IP、端口、时序、大小、无 TLS 时的明文协议，以及可能的 HTTP 元数据。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Malicious proxy client"
msgstr "恶意代理客户端"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Send malformed/replayed/authentication-failing traffic and consume server "
"resources."
msgstr "发送格式错误、重放或认证失败流量，并消耗服务端资源。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Malicious/compromised proxy server"
msgstr "恶意/被攻陷的代理服务端"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Observe target destinations and plaintext after proxy decryption, return "
"malicious content, manipulate DNS/routing behavior under its control."
msgstr ""
"观察代理解密后的目标地址和明文、返回恶意内容，并操纵其控制范围内的 DNS/"
"routing 行为。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Reverse proxy/CDN/logging infrastructure"
msgstr "反向代理/CDN/日志基础设施"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Observe HTTP/XHTTP/gRPC metadata that is outside end-to-end encrypted inner "
"payloads."
msgstr "观察不属于端到端加密内层负载的 HTTP/XHTTP/gRPC 元数据。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Privileged local attacker"
msgstr "本地特权攻击者"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Control service/core lifecycle, routes, DNS, TUN, process memory, and "
"configuration; protocol cryptography cannot protect against full local "
"privilege compromise."
msgstr ""
"控制 service/core 生命周期、路由、DNS、TUN、进程内存和配置；协议密码学无法抵"
"御完整的本地特权失陷。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "The appropriate mitigation depends on which actor is in scope."
msgstr "合适的缓解措施取决于威胁模型中包含哪类攻击者。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Local Proxy Listeners Are Security Boundaries"
msgstr "本地代理 Listener 也是安全边界"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"SOCKS5, local HTTP proxy, and mixed listeners are often plaintext "
"application-facing interfaces. If exposed beyond the intended host, they can "
"become open proxies or leak credentials/traffic metadata."
msgstr ""
"SOCKS5、本地 HTTP proxy 和 mixed listener 通常是面向应用的明文接口。如果暴露"
"到预期主机之外，它们可能变成开放代理，或泄漏凭据/流量元数据。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "For local-only desktop use:"
msgstr "对于仅本机使用的桌面部署："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "prefer loopback binding unless LAN access is intentionally required;"
msgstr "除非确实需要 LAN 访问，否则优先绑定 loopback；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "verify `allow-lan`/source policy and actual bind address;"
msgstr "检查 `allow-lan`/来源策略和真实 bind address；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"use listener authentication where the implementation and deployment require "
"shared access;"
msgstr "实现和部署需要共享访问时，为 listener 使用认证；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"firewall LAN/WAN access even when the application configuration appears "
"restrictive;"
msgstr "即使应用配置看起来已经限制访问，也应通过 firewall 限制 LAN/WAN；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"do not assume remote-protocol authentication protects the local listener."
msgstr "不要假设远程协议认证会保护本地 listener。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"A LAN peer that can use your local SOCKS listener does not need to know your "
"remote VLESS UUID or Shadowsocks key; your Client will authenticate to the "
"remote server on its behalf."
msgstr ""
"能够使用你本地 SOCKS listener 的 LAN 对端不需要知道远程 VLESS UUID 或 "
"Shadowsocks 密钥；Client 会代表它向远端服务端完成认证。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Chimera_Client Controller/API"
msgstr "Chimera_Client Controller/API"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"The Client controller is a control and observation surface, not a public "
"application proxy."
msgstr "Client controller 是控制与观测接口，不是公开的应用代理。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Current TCP API behavior requires a bearer token when a secret is "
"configured, and the Client rejects unsafe non-loopback TCP API exposure "
"without a secret. Non-loopback API exposure also requires explicit valid "
"CORS origins."
msgstr ""
"当前 TCP API 在配置 secret 后要求 bearer token，并会拒绝没有 secret 的不安全"
"非 loopback TCP API 暴露。非 loopback API 暴露还要求显式有效的 CORS origin。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Security guidance:"
msgstr "安全建议："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"keep the controller on loopback unless remote administration is genuinely "
"needed;"
msgstr "除非确实需要远程管理，否则让 controller 保持在 loopback；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "configure a high-entropy secret before non-loopback exposure;"
msgstr "暴露到非 loopback 前配置高熵 secret；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"restrict it with host firewall rules in addition to application "
"authentication;"
msgstr "除应用认证外，再使用主机 firewall 规则限制访问；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"do not put bearer secrets in screenshots, logs, shell history, or bug "
"reports;"
msgstr "不要在截图、日志、shell history 或 bug report 中放入 bearer secret；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"remember that `/connections`, `/proxies`, `/configs`, DNS queries, logs, and "
"traffic information can reveal sensitive operational metadata even without "
"raw payloads."
msgstr ""
"即使没有原始负载，也要记住 `/connections`、`/proxies`、`/configs`、DNS "
"query、日志和流量信息可能暴露敏感运维元数据。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"A compromised controller can expose much more than a passive packet capture."
msgstr "controller 被攻陷后可能暴露的内容远多于被动抓包。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Service Mode and Privileged IPC"
msgstr "Service Mode 与特权 IPC"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"`Chimera_Service` can start, stop, and restart selected cores using supplied "
"configuration paths, report runtime status, and perform supported privileged "
"network operations such as DNS changes."
msgstr ""
"`Chimera_Service` 可以使用提供的配置路径启动、停止和重启所选 core，报告运行状"
"态，并执行受支持的特权网络操作，例如修改 DNS。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "That makes the Desktop → Service IPC boundary security-sensitive."
msgstr "因此 Desktop → Service IPC 边界具有安全敏感性。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Operational requirements include:"
msgstr "运维要求包括："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"rely on the repository's local IPC ACL/security mechanisms rather than "
"exposing the service control endpoint broadly;"
msgstr ""
"依赖仓库提供的本地 IPC ACL/安全机制，而不是广泛暴露 service 控制 endpoint；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"keep Desktop, Service, shared IPC types, and core binaries from trusted "
"build/update sources;"
msgstr ""
"确保 Desktop、Service、共享 IPC type 和 core 二进制来自可信构建/更新来源；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"treat a config path supplied to a privileged service as security-sensitive "
"input;"
msgstr "把提交给特权 service 的配置路径视为安全敏感输入；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "avoid world-writable generated-config directories;"
msgstr "避免使用全局可写的生成配置目录；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "verify service-account file permissions and executable paths;"
msgstr "检查 service account 的文件权限和可执行文件路径；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"distinguish service-process compromise from proxy-core compromise in "
"incident response."
msgstr "事故响应中区分 service 进程失陷和 proxy core 失陷。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Service mode increases operational privilege; it does not strengthen proxy "
"protocol authentication by itself."
msgstr "Service mode 会提高运维权限，但本身不会增强代理协议认证。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Android VPN/TUN Boundary"
msgstr "Android VPN/TUN 边界"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"`AChimera` owns an Android `VpnService` and passes the TUN file descriptor "
"to the embedded Rust core. The `protect(fd)` callback prevents the proxy "
"core's own remote sockets from being captured by the VPN again."
msgstr ""
"`AChimera` 持有 Android `VpnService`，并把 TUN 文件描述符传给内嵌 Rust core。"
"`protect(fd)` 回调用于避免代理 core 自己的远程 socket 再次被 VPN 捕获。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Security/reliability concerns include:"
msgstr "安全/可靠性风险包括："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"incorrect route or DNS configuration can leak traffic outside the intended "
"VPN path;"
msgstr "错误的路由或 DNS 配置可能让流量泄漏到预期 VPN 路径之外；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"failure to protect proxy sockets can create loops or unexpected routing;"
msgstr "未能 protect 代理 socket 可能造成循环或非预期路由；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"per-app include/exclude policy changes which applications are inside the "
"trust boundary;"
msgstr "按应用 include/exclude 策略会改变哪些应用处于该信任边界内；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"profile files and remote subscription metadata remain sensitive application "
"data;"
msgstr "profile 文件和远程订阅元数据仍属于敏感应用数据；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Android VPN permission proves user authorization to create the VPN, not "
"remote proxy identity."
msgstr "Android VPN 权限只证明用户授权创建 VPN，并不能证明远程代理身份。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"When the same profile behaves differently on desktop and Android, do not "
"immediately weaken TLS/protocol checks to make Android work. Prove the VPN/"
"TUN/protection path first."
msgstr ""
"同一 profile 在桌面与 Android 表现不同时，不要为了让 Android 能工作就立即削"
"弱 TLS/协议检查；应先证明 VPN/TUN/protection 路径正常。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "DNS Privacy and Routing Leaks"
msgstr "DNS 隐私与路由泄漏"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"A proxy can carry application traffic while DNS still leaves through an "
"unintended resolver."
msgstr "即使应用流量已经走代理，DNS 仍可能通过非预期 resolver 离开。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Leak risks include:"
msgstr "泄漏风险包括："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "application resolves locally before using a proxy;"
msgstr "应用在使用代理前先进行了本地解析；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "system DNS bypasses the Client DNS listener;"
msgstr "系统 DNS 绕过 Client DNS listener；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "TUN captures traffic but DNS hijack/routing does not match;"
msgstr "TUN 已捕获流量，但 DNS hijack/routing 没有匹配；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Fake-IP reverse mapping fails and routing falls back unexpectedly;"
msgstr "Fake-IP 反向映射失败并导致 routing 意外回退；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"server-side domain resolution reveals destinations to the server's resolver "
"even when the client used remote-domain semantics."
msgstr ""
"即使客户端使用远程域名语义，服务端侧域名解析仍会向服务端 resolver 暴露目标。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Decide explicitly **where names should be resolved** and test that path. DNS "
"privacy is not automatically provided by SOCKS5, HTTP CONNECT, or a remote "
"encrypted proxy protocol."
msgstr ""
"应显式决定**域名应该在哪里解析**并测试该路径。SOCKS5、HTTP CONNECT 或远程加密"
"代理协议都不会自动提供 DNS 隐私。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "TUN and Transparent Routing Risks"
msgstr "TUN 与透明路由风险"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"TUN, redir, TProxy, and Dokodemo `followRedirect` move policy into operating-"
"system routing/firewall state."
msgstr ""
"TUN、redir、TProxy 和 Dokodemo `followRedirect` 会把部分策略移动到操作系统 "
"routing/firewall 状态中。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Common risks are:"
msgstr "常见风险包括："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "traffic bypass because a route/table/rule is missing;"
msgstr "因为缺少 route/table/rule 导致流量绕过；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "routing loops;"
msgstr "路由环路；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "DNS escaping through an interface not covered by policy;"
msgstr "DNS 通过策略未覆盖的接口泄漏；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "accidentally capturing the proxy server connection itself;"
msgstr "意外捕获代理服务端连接本身；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "exposing a transparent listener to networks that should never reach it;"
msgstr "把透明 listener 暴露给本不应访问它的网络；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"assuming `followRedirect` creates interception rules when it only consumes "
"original-destination metadata."
msgstr ""
"误以为 `followRedirect` 会创建拦截规则，实际上它只消费 original-destination "
"元数据。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Treat OS routes/firewall state as part of the security configuration, not as "
"an implementation detail outside the proxy."
msgstr ""
"应把操作系统 route/firewall 状态视为安全配置的一部分，而不是代理之外无关紧要"
"的实现细节。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Remote Listener Exposure"
msgstr "远程 Listener 暴露"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"A server listener should expose only the protocol/transport actually "
"intended for remote clients."
msgstr "服务端 listener 应只暴露真正需要提供给远程客户端的协议/传输。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Controls include:"
msgstr "控制措施包括："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "bind only required addresses/interfaces;"
msgstr "只绑定需要的地址/接口；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "firewall only required TCP/UDP ports;"
msgstr "只在 firewall 放行需要的 TCP/UDP 端口；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "remove obsolete inbounds and fallback listeners;"
msgstr "删除已废弃的 inbound 和 fallback listener；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"avoid exposing management APIs on the same trust level as public proxy "
"inbounds;"
msgstr "避免把管理 API 暴露在与公共代理 inbound 相同的信任级别；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "verify IPv6 exposure separately from IPv4;"
msgstr "分别验证 IPv6 与 IPv4 暴露情况；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "treat QUIC/UDP reachability as a separate firewall surface from TCP."
msgstr "把 QUIC/UDP 可达性视为独立于 TCP 的 firewall 攻击面。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"A protocol's authentication failure behavior matters only after the attacker "
"can reach the listener."
msgstr "只有攻击者已经能够到达 listener 后，协议的认证失败行为才开始发挥作用。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "TLS Security"
msgstr "TLS 安全"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "For TLS-based transports/protocols:"
msgstr "对于基于 TLS 的传输/协议："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"keep certificate verification enabled on clients unless there is a "
"documented private trust model;"
msgstr "除非有明确记录的私有信任模型，否则客户端保持证书验证开启；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "validate SNI/server names deliberately;"
msgstr "有意识地验证 SNI/server name；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "protect server private keys with restrictive file permissions;"
msgstr "使用严格文件权限保护服务端私钥；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "rotate certificates/keys according to deployment policy;"
msgstr "按部署策略轮换证书/密钥；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "provide client certificate/key together when mTLS is required;"
msgstr "需要 mTLS 时同时提供客户端证书/私钥；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"keep ALPN aligned with the transport (`h2` is required by the current Server "
"gRPC/TLS path)."
msgstr "保持 ALPN 与传输一致（当前 Server gRPC/TLS 路径要求 `h2`）。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"`skip-cert-verify` is a security downgrade, not a generic troubleshooting "
"switch. If disabling it makes a connection work, fix the trust/SNI/"
"certificate problem rather than leaving verification off."
msgstr ""
"`skip-cert-verify` 是安全降级，不是通用排障开关。如果关闭验证后连接才能工作，"
"应修复 trust/SNI/证书问题，而不是长期保持验证关闭。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "REALITY Security Boundary"
msgstr "REALITY 安全边界"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"REALITY adds a transport-security/camouflage mechanism but does not replace "
"the inner proxy account/flow checks."
msgstr "REALITY 增加传输安全/伪装机制，但不会替代内层代理账户/flow 检查。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Protect:"
msgstr "应保护："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "the REALITY private key;"
msgstr "REALITY 私钥；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "expected server names;"
msgstr "预期 server name；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "short IDs;"
msgstr "short ID；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "VLESS UUID/flow configuration separately."
msgstr "并单独保护/管理 VLESS UUID/flow 配置。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Current Server tests deliberately cover cases where wrong server name, short "
"ID, public key, client version, VLESS UUID, or Vision flow fail "
"independently."
msgstr ""
"当前 Server 测试刻意覆盖 server name、short ID、公钥、客户端版本、VLESS UUID "
"或 Vision flow 各自独立错误的情况。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Fallback behavior is part of the security design. A mismatch may route "
"traffic to the configured REALITY destination rather than simply closing. "
"Ensure that destination is safe to expose and that fallback cannot be abused "
"to reach an unintended internal service."
msgstr ""
"Fallback 行为是安全设计的一部分。发生不匹配时，流量可能被路由到已配置的 "
"REALITY destination，而不是简单关闭。应确保该目标适合暴露，并避免 fallback 被"
"滥用来访问非预期内部服务。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Shadowsocks Security"
msgstr "Shadowsocks 安全"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "For classic AEAD:"
msgstr "对于经典 AEAD："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "use modern AEAD methods supported by both peers;"
msgstr "使用双方都支持的现代 AEAD 方法；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "protect passwords/master keys;"
msgstr "保护密码/master key；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "never reuse salt/nonce material deliberately;"
msgstr "不要主动复用 salt/nonce 材料；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "keep replay defenses enabled."
msgstr "保持重放防护开启。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "For AEAD-2022:"
msgstr "对于 AEAD-2022："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"the current Server treats configured Base64 material as raw PSK and enforces "
"exact key length;"
msgstr "当前 Server 把配置的 Base64 内容视为原始 PSK，并强制精确密钥长度；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "timestamp validation makes clock synchronization relevant;"
msgstr "时间戳验证使时钟同步变得重要；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "session/packet replay windows are active security state;"
msgstr "session/packet 重放窗口属于真实生效的安全状态；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"multi-user EIH changes user selection and must use supported method "
"combinations."
msgstr "多用户 EIH 会改变用户选择流程，必须使用受支持的方法组合。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Do not advertise a Client-only cipher as Server-compatible without "
"interoperability evidence."
msgstr "没有互操作证据时，不要把仅 Client 支持的 cipher 宣称为 Server 兼容。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "AnyTLS Security"
msgstr "AnyTLS 安全"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "AnyTLS uses two distinct layers:"
msgstr "AnyTLS 使用两个独立层次："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "TLS for encrypted transport/server identity;"
msgstr "TLS 用于加密传输/服务端身份；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"a deterministic 32-byte `SHA256(password)` authentication token inside TLS."
msgstr "TLS 内部使用确定性的 32 字节 `SHA256(password)` 认证令牌。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Use a high-entropy password and keep TLS certificate verification enabled. "
"The password hash is not a substitute for server certificate authentication."
msgstr "使用高熵密码并保持 TLS 证书验证开启。密码哈希不能替代服务端证书认证。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"The current Client inbound can send unknown-password traffic to a configured "
"fallback **after TLS termination**. That fallback receives decrypted TLS "
"application bytes. Point it only at a service intentionally designed to "
"receive such traffic."
msgstr ""
"当前 Client 入站可以在 **TLS 终止之后**把未知密码流量送到配置的 fallback。该 "
"fallback 会收到已经解密的 TLS 应用字节，因此只能指向有意设计来接收此类流量的"
"服务。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Parsed-only fingerprint/idle-session fields must not be relied upon as "
"active security controls in the current runtime."
msgstr ""
"不能把 Parsed-only 的 fingerprint/idle-session 字段当作当前运行时真正生效的安"
"全控制。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Trojan Security"
msgstr "Trojan 安全"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Trojan depends on TLS plus its password-based proxy authentication. Protect "
"both layers independently."
msgstr "Trojan 依赖 TLS 和基于密码的代理认证；两个层次都应独立保护。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Fallback rules are security-sensitive because unauthenticated or mismatched "
"traffic can be intentionally routed elsewhere. Validate fallback "
"destination, path/type rules, and which fields are actually implemented by "
"Chimera Server."
msgstr ""
"Fallback 规则具有安全敏感性，因为未认证或不匹配流量可能被有意路由到其他位置。"
"应验证 fallback destination、path/type 规则以及 Chimera Server 真正实现了哪些"
"字段。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"A safe fallback target should not be an unauthenticated administrative or "
"internal-only service merely because it is convenient for camouflage."
msgstr ""
"安全的 fallback 目标不应仅为了伪装方便就指向未认证的管理服务或内部专用服务。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "VLESS and VMess Security"
msgstr "VLESS 与 VMess 安全"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"A VLESS UUID identifies/authorizes a proxy user but basic VLESS does not by "
"itself provide transport confidentiality. Use the intended VLESS Encryption "
"and/or TLS/REALITY stack according to the deployment design."
msgstr ""
"VLESS UUID 用于标识/授权代理用户，但基础 VLESS 本身不提供传输机密性。应根据部"
"署设计使用预期的 VLESS Encryption 和/或 TLS/REALITY 协议栈。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Keep flow mode and transport compatibility explicit; changing Vision/plain "
"flow to bypass an error can change the security and traffic-shaping model."
msgstr ""
"应明确 flow 模式和传输兼容性；为了绕过错误而切换 Vision/plain flow 可能改变安"
"全和流量形态模型。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"VMess AEAD provides its own authenticated/encrypted request/body records and "
"anti-replay/time-related state. Protect user IDs and do not re-enable "
"historical insecure modes merely for compatibility."
msgstr ""
"VMess AEAD 自身提供经过认证/加密的请求与正文记录，以及防重放/时间相关状态。应"
"保护用户 ID，不要仅为兼容而重新启用历史不安全模式。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"For both protocols, outer transport camouflage is separate from inner proxy "
"authentication."
msgstr "对于这两个协议，外层传输伪装与内层代理认证是相互独立的。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Hysteria 2 and TUIC Security"
msgstr "Hysteria 2 与 TUIC 安全"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Hysteria 2 and TUIC build on QUIC/TLS and add their own proxy authentication/"
"session semantics."
msgstr ""
"Hysteria 2 与 TUIC 建立在 QUIC/TLS 之上，并增加各自的代理认证/会话语义。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Security/resource considerations include:"
msgstr "安全/资源方面需要考虑："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "UDP listener exposure and firewall policy;"
msgstr "UDP listener 暴露和 firewall 策略；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "credential protection;"
msgstr "凭据保护；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "QUIC handshake/resource cost under unauthenticated floods;"
msgstr "未认证洪泛下的 QUIC 握手/资源成本；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "limits on concurrent streams/sessions/associations;"
msgstr "并发 stream/session/association 限制；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "UDP amplification/resource abuse against reachable targets;"
msgstr "针对可达目标的 UDP 放大/资源滥用；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "idle/session cleanup;"
msgstr "idle/session 清理；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "target-routing policy."
msgstr "目标路由策略。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Do not apply TCP-only rate/connection assumptions to a public QUIC listener."
msgstr "不要把只适用于 TCP 的速率/连接假设套用到公开 QUIC listener。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "XHTTP Metadata Exposure"
msgstr "XHTTP 元数据暴露"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"XHTTP can place session IDs, sequence numbers, padding metadata, and "
"sometimes uplink data chunks in HTTP-visible structures such as paths, query "
"strings, headers, or cookies depending on configuration."
msgstr ""
"根据配置，XHTTP 可以把 session ID、sequence number、padding 元数据，有时还有"
"上行数据块，放入 path、query string、header 或 cookie 等 HTTP 可见结构。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Even when the inner proxy stream is encrypted/authenticated, infrastructure "
"around the HTTP layer may log metadata:"
msgstr "即使内层代理流已经加密/认证，HTTP 层周围的基础设施仍可能记录元数据："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "reverse proxy access logs;"
msgstr "反向代理访问日志；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "CDN/WAF logs;"
msgstr "CDN/WAF 日志；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "HTTP header/query tracing;"
msgstr "HTTP header/query tracing；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "browser/developer tooling in unusual deployments."
msgstr "特殊部署中的浏览器/开发工具。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Avoid putting reusable secrets into configurable XHTTP metadata keys/values. "
"Review logging retention and redaction when using header/cookie/query "
"placement."
msgstr ""
"避免把可复用秘密放入可配置 XHTTP 元数据 key/value。使用 header/cookie/query "
"放置方式时，应审查日志保留与脱敏策略。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"`Host`, path, padding, and session metadata are transport validation/"
"camouflage, not a replacement for inner proxy authentication."
msgstr ""
"`Host`、path、padding 和 session 元数据属于传输验证/伪装，不能替代内层代理认"
"证。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "gRPC and HTTPUpgrade Metadata"
msgstr "gRPC 与 HTTPUpgrade 元数据"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"gRPC transport exposes service path, HTTP/2 metadata, timing, and message "
"sizes to any infrastructure that can see the HTTP layer. TLS/REALITY can "
"protect this on the network, but a terminating reverse proxy can still "
"observe HTTP metadata."
msgstr ""
"gRPC 传输会向能够看到 HTTP 层的基础设施暴露 service path、HTTP/2 元数据、时序"
"和消息大小。TLS/REALITY 可以保护网络链路，但终止 TLS 的反向代理仍可观察 HTTP "
"元数据。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"HTTPUpgrade's `Host`, path, and `Upgrade` headers likewise provide transport "
"matching/camouflage rather than cryptographic authentication. After `101`, "
"current Chimera HTTPUpgrade carries raw inner-protocol bytes rather than "
"WebSocket frames."
msgstr ""
"HTTPUpgrade 的 `Host`、path 和 `Upgrade` header 同样提供传输匹配/伪装，而不是"
"密码学认证。`101` 之后，当前 Chimera HTTPUpgrade 承载原始内层协议字节，而不"
"是 WebSocket frame。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Do not confuse “request reached the correct path” with “proxy user "
"authenticated”."
msgstr "不要把“请求到达正确 path”与“代理用户已认证”混为一谈。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Dokodemo-door Is Not an Authenticated Proxy"
msgstr "Dokodemo-door 不是带认证的代理"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Dokodemo-door has no user-authentication handshake of its own."
msgstr "Dokodemo-door 自身没有用户认证握手。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"A fixed-target Dokodemo listener exposed to an untrusted network can act as "
"a direct port forward to the configured service. Protect it with bind scope, "
"firewall policy, outer security where appropriate, and target-service "
"authentication."
msgstr ""
"固定目标 Dokodemo listener 若暴露到不可信网络，就可能成为通往配置服务的直接端"
"口转发。应使用 bind 范围、firewall 策略、适用的外层安全机制和目标服务认证保护"
"它。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"For Linux `followRedirect`, the OS interception rules determine which "
"traffic enters the listener. A broad or incorrect redirect rule is a "
"security policy bug even if the Rust handler behaves exactly as designed."
msgstr ""
"对于 Linux `followRedirect`，由操作系统拦截规则决定哪些流量进入 listener。即"
"使 Rust handler 完全按设计运行，过宽或错误的 redirect 规则仍属于安全策略漏"
"洞。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Fallback Safety"
msgstr "Fallback 安全"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Fallback is not just a compatibility feature. It changes what "
"unauthenticated, malformed, or camouflage traffic can reach."
msgstr ""
"Fallback 不只是兼容功能，它会改变未认证、格式错误或伪装流量最终能够访问的目"
"标。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "For every fallback path, document:"
msgstr "对每条 fallback 路径都应记录："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "triggering condition;"
msgstr "触发条件；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "destination service;"
msgstr "目标服务；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"whether bytes are raw encrypted transport bytes or already-decrypted "
"application bytes;"
msgstr "流量是原始加密传输字节，还是已经解密的应用字节；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "whether original SNI/path metadata is preserved;"
msgstr "原始 SNI/path 元数据是否保留；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "whether the target service requires its own authentication;"
msgstr "目标服务是否需要自身认证；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "whether an attacker can intentionally trigger fallback repeatedly."
msgstr "攻击者是否可以反复主动触发 fallback。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"The Server E2E suite contains fallback cases because “reject” and “route to "
"fallback” are materially different security outcomes."
msgstr ""
"Server E2E 套件包含 fallback 场景，因为“拒绝”和“路由到 fallback”在安全结果上"
"有本质区别。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "UDP and Amplification/Resource Abuse"
msgstr "UDP 与放大/资源滥用"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Public UDP/QUIC listeners need resource controls independent of TCP controls."
msgstr "公开 UDP/QUIC listener 需要独立于 TCP 控制之外的资源控制。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Threats include:"
msgstr "威胁包括："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "spoofed-source traffic where the network permits it;"
msgstr "在网络允许源地址伪造时的 spoofed-source 流量；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "high-rate unauthenticated QUIC handshakes;"
msgstr "高频未认证 QUIC 握手；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "creating many protocol associations/sessions;"
msgstr "创建大量协议 association/session；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "sending traffic toward high-amplification targets;"
msgstr "向高放大目标发送流量；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "retaining idle UDP state too long;"
msgstr "空闲 UDP 状态保留过久；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "oversized datagrams or fragmentation pressure."
msgstr "超大数据报或分片压力。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Use firewall/rate controls, protocol authentication, bounded session state, "
"idle expiry, and routing restrictions appropriate to the deployment."
msgstr ""
"应根据部署使用 firewall/速率控制、协议认证、有界 session 状态、空闲过期和路由"
"限制。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Current implementations already contain protocol-specific replay/session/"
"timeout controls in several paths, but those do not replace network-level "
"abuse controls."
msgstr ""
"当前多个实现路径已经包含协议特有的重放/session/timeout 控制，但它们不能替代网"
"络层面的滥用防护。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Logging and Redaction"
msgstr "日志与脱敏"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Logs are valuable for troubleshooting and can also become a data leak."
msgstr "日志对故障排查很有价值，但同样可能成为数据泄漏来源。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Do not log or publish:"
msgstr "不要记录或公开："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "raw passwords/PSKs/private keys;"
msgstr "原始密码/PSK/私钥；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "controller bearer secrets;"
msgstr "controller bearer secret；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "full subscription URLs containing tokens;"
msgstr "包含 token 的完整订阅 URL；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "complete generated configs without sanitization;"
msgstr "未经脱敏的完整生成配置；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"authentication tokens or deterministic password hashes when they can be "
"reused;"
msgstr "可复用的认证 token 或确定性密码哈希；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "sensitive DNS/target history beyond the required operational retention."
msgstr "超出必要运维保留周期的敏感 DNS/目标历史。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Be careful with structured logs containing target addresses, inbound tags, "
"user identities, SNI, XHTTP metadata, and connection chains. Decide "
"retention and access policy deliberately."
msgstr ""
"包含目标地址、inbound tag、用户身份、SNI、XHTTP 元数据和连接链的结构化日志需"
"要谨慎处理，并明确制定保留与访问策略。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Configuration and File Permissions"
msgstr "配置与文件权限"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Generated configuration often contains everything needed to authenticate as "
"the user."
msgstr "生成配置往往包含以该用户身份完成认证所需的全部材料。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "profile directories;"
msgstr "profile 目录；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "generated runtime YAML/JSON5;"
msgstr "生成的运行时 YAML/JSON5；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "TLS/REALITY key files;"
msgstr "TLS/REALITY 密钥文件；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "service data/config directories;"
msgstr "service 数据/配置目录；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "test fixtures containing real secrets;"
msgstr "包含真实秘密的测试 fixture；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "backups and crash reports."
msgstr "备份和崩溃报告。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Use placeholders or dedicated test credentials in repository examples. Never "
"copy production credentials into an interoperability test merely to make it "
"realistic."
msgstr ""
"仓库示例应使用占位符或专用测试凭据。不要仅为了让互操作测试看起来更真实，就把"
"生产凭据复制进去。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Updates and Build Provenance"
msgstr "更新与构建来源"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"The ecosystem can run different core binaries and optional Cargo feature "
"sets. Security review must therefore identify the **actual artifact**, not "
"only the repository source."
msgstr ""
"该生态可以运行不同 core 二进制和不同可选 Cargo feature 集。因此安全审查必须确"
"认**实际部署的构建产物**，而不能只看仓库源码。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Record:"
msgstr "应记录："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "core type;"
msgstr "core 类型；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "version/commit;"
msgstr "版本/commit；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "enabled optional protocol features;"
msgstr "已启用的可选协议 feature；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "update source/channel;"
msgstr "更新来源/channel；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "checksum/signature verification process where available."
msgstr "可用时的 checksum/签名验证流程。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"A protocol implementation existing in source does not prove the deployed "
"binary contains it, and a security fix in source does not protect an older "
"deployed binary."
msgstr ""
"源码中存在某协议实现，并不能证明已部署二进制包含它；源码中的安全修复也无法保"
"护尚未更新的旧二进制。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Deployment Baseline"
msgstr "部署基线"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "A reasonable baseline for an Internet-facing deployment is:"
msgstr "一个合理的互联网暴露部署基线是："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"bind local Client/controller listeners to loopback unless remote access is "
"required;"
msgstr ""
"除非需要远程访问，否则把本地 Client/controller listener 绑定到 loopback；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "firewall Server ports to only the required TCP/UDP surface;"
msgstr "通过 firewall 只开放 Server 必需的 TCP/UDP 攻击面；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "enable and validate protocol authentication;"
msgstr "启用并验证协议认证；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "enable TLS/REALITY where the protocol/transport design requires it;"
msgstr "在协议/传输设计需要时启用 TLS/REALITY；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "keep certificate verification enabled;"
msgstr "保持证书验证开启；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "protect credentials and generated config files;"
msgstr "保护凭据和生成配置文件；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "verify DNS/TUN routing does not bypass policy;"
msgstr "验证 DNS/TUN routing 不会绕过策略；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "review all fallback destinations;"
msgstr "审查所有 fallback 目标；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "bound UDP/QUIC/session resources;"
msgstr "限制 UDP/QUIC/session 资源；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "redact logs and bug reports;"
msgstr "对日志和 bug report 做脱敏；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"run the strongest relevant negative/interoperability tests after security-"
"sensitive changes."
msgstr "完成安全敏感改动后，运行最强的相关负向/互操作测试。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"This baseline is intentionally layered. No single checkbox replaces the "
"others."
msgstr "该基线有意采用分层设计，任何一个单独选项都不能替代其他层。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Security Review Checklist"
msgstr "安全审查清单"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Before exposing a new inbound or client control surface, answer:"
msgstr "暴露新的 inbound 或客户端控制接口前，应回答："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Who can connect to it at the network layer?"
msgstr "网络层面谁能够连接它？"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "What authenticates that peer?"
msgstr "什么机制认证该对端？"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Is the channel encrypted, and who terminates encryption?"
msgstr "通道是否加密，由谁终止加密？"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "What metadata remains visible outside encryption?"
msgstr "加密之外仍有哪些元数据可见？"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "What happens on authentication failure: close, drop, or fallback?"
msgstr "认证失败时会发生什么：关闭、丢弃还是 fallback？"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Can the caller choose an arbitrary destination?"
msgstr "调用方能否选择任意目标地址？"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Can UDP/QUIC behavior be abused for resource consumption or amplification?"
msgstr "UDP/QUIC 行为能否被滥用于资源消耗或放大攻击？"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "Which secrets/config files are readable by the process and local users?"
msgstr "进程和本地用户能够读取哪些秘密/配置文件？"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "What is logged?"
msgstr "会记录哪些日志？"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"Which negative tests prove malformed/unauthorized traffic is handled as "
"expected?"
msgstr "哪些负向测试证明格式错误/未授权流量会按预期处理？"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"If any answer is unknown, treat it as an unresolved deployment risk rather "
"than assuming a protocol name implies safety."
msgstr ""
"如果任一答案未知，应把它视为尚未解决的部署风险，而不是因为使用了某个协议名称"
"就默认安全。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"The implementation-specific boundaries in this page are derived from the "
"current source and documentation work around:"
msgstr "本页中的实现特定边界来自当前源码与以下文档审计工作："

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"`Chimera_Client` listener/API authorization, DNS/TUN, optional protocol "
"features, AnyTLS and Shadowsocks implementations;"
msgstr ""
"`Chimera_Client` listener/API 授权、DNS/TUN、可选协议 feature，以及 AnyTLS "
"和 Shadowsocks 实现；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "`Chimera_Service` IPC/ACL and privileged core/network management;"
msgstr "`Chimera_Service` IPC/ACL 与特权 core/网络管理；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid "`AChimera` `VpnService`, TUN ownership, and `protect(fd)` bridge;"
msgstr "`AChimera` 的 `VpnService`、TUN 所有权和 `protect(fd)` 桥接；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"`Chimera_Server` config validation, fallback handling, protocol/transport "
"handlers, replay/session state, routing, and tests;"
msgstr ""
"`Chimera_Server` 配置验证、fallback 处理、协议/传输 handler、重放/session 状"
"态、routing 与测试；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"protocol chapters in this Wiki that document current wire/security behavior;"
msgstr "本 Wiki 中记录当前线协议/安全行为的各协议章节；"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"negative and interoperability suites catalogued in [Test Evidence and "
"Interoperability Matrix](./test-evidence.md)."
msgstr ""
"以及 [测试证据与互操作矩阵](./test-evidence.md) 中整理的负向和互操作测试套"
"件。"

#: src/security-model.md
msgid ""
"When a field moves from Parsed-only/Rejected to active runtime behavior, or "
"when a new listener/control endpoint is added, re-evaluate the corresponding "
"trust boundary here."
msgstr ""
"当字段从 Parsed-only/Rejected 变为实际运行时行为，或新增 listener/control "
"endpoint 时，应重新评估本页对应的信任边界。"

#: src/chimera_client.md
msgid "Role and Source of Truth"
msgstr "角色与事实来源"

#: src/chimera_client.md
msgid ""
"`Chimera_Client` is the Clash-compatible client runtime in the Chimera "
"ecosystem. It parses Clash-style configuration, exposes local proxy "
"listeners, performs DNS/rule dispatch, and creates remote outbound "
"connections."
msgstr ""
"`Chimera_Client` 是 Chimera 生态中的 Clash 兼容客户端运行时。它解析 Clash 风"
"格配置、提供本地代理监听器、执行 DNS/规则分发，并建立远程出站连接。"

#: src/chimera_client.md
msgid ""
"For implementation status, the source tree is authoritative. In particular:"
msgstr "实现状态以源码树为准，尤其应检查："

#: src/chimera_client.md
msgid ""
"`clash-lib/src/config/internal/proxy.rs` defines the current outbound "
"protocol configuration enum."
msgstr "`clash-lib/src/config/internal/proxy.rs` 定义当前出站协议配置枚举。"

#: src/chimera_client.md
msgid ""
"`clash-lib/src/app/outbound/manager.rs` registers concrete outbound handlers."
msgstr "`clash-lib/src/app/outbound/manager.rs` 注册具体出站处理器。"

#: src/chimera_client.md
msgid ""
"`clash-lib/src/proxy/` contains protocol, inbound, outbound, and transport "
"implementations."
msgstr "`clash-lib/src/proxy/` 包含协议、入站、出站与传输实现。"

#: src/chimera_client.md
msgid ""
"`clash-lib/Cargo.toml` determines which optional implementations are present "
"in a given binary."
msgstr "`clash-lib/Cargo.toml` 决定某个二进制中包含哪些可选实现。"

#: src/chimera_client.md
msgid ""
"See [Implementation Status and Source Evidence](./implementation-status.md) "
"for the evidence terminology used by this Wiki."
msgstr ""
"本 Wiki 使用的证据术语见 [Implementation Status and Source Evidence](./"
"implementation-status.md)。"

