msgstr "RFC 1928（全文）"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"An HTTP proxy is an application-level proxy used by browsers, command-line "
"tools, package managers, and operating-system proxy settings. For ordinary "
"HTTP requests, the client sends the request through the proxy. For HTTPS and "
"other TCP destinations, the client normally asks the proxy to create a "
"tunnel with the HTTP `CONNECT` method."
msgstr ""
"HTTP 代理是一种应用层代理，常用于浏览器、命令行工具、包管理器和操作系统代理设"
"置。对于普通 HTTP 请求，客户端通过代理发送请求；对于 HTTPS 和其他 TCP 目标，"
"客户端通常使用 HTTP `CONNECT` 方法要求代理建立隧道。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"HTTP proxying should not be confused with XHTTP. An HTTP proxy is an inbound "
"proxy protocol used by local applications; [XHTTP](../transports/xhttp.md) "
"is an Xray transport used between compatible proxy endpoints."
msgstr ""
"HTTP 代理不应与 XHTTP 混淆。HTTP 代理是本地应用使用的入站代理协议；[XHTTP](./"
"xhttp.md) 则是兼容代理端点之间使用的一种 Xray 传输方式。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "Plain HTTP request"
msgstr "普通 HTTP 请求"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "The client connects to the HTTP proxy."
msgstr "客户端连接到 HTTP 代理。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "The client sends a normal HTTP request using an absolute target URI."
msgstr "客户端使用绝对目标 URI 发送普通 HTTP 请求。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "The proxy applies authentication and routing policy."
msgstr "代理应用认证和路由策略。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"The proxy sends the request to the origin server and relays the response."
msgstr "代理把请求发送到源站，并把响应转发给客户端。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "`CONNECT` tunnel"
msgstr "`CONNECT` 隧道"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "The client sends a request such as `CONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1`."
msgstr "客户端发送类似 `CONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1` 的请求。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "The proxy validates the target and access policy."
msgstr "代理验证目标和访问策略。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "The proxy establishes a TCP connection to the requested destination."
msgstr "代理与请求的目标建立 TCP 连接。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "After a successful response, the proxy relays bytes in both directions."
msgstr "返回成功响应后，代理开始双向转发字节流。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "For HTTPS, the end-to-end TLS handshake happens inside that tunnel."
msgstr "对于 HTTPS，端到端 TLS 握手会发生在该隧道内部。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"The `CONNECT` method creates a TCP-oriented tunnel. It does not by itself "
"add UDP proxying."
msgstr "`CONNECT` 方法创建的是面向 TCP 的隧道，本身并不会增加 UDP 代理能力。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "CONNECT on the Wire"
msgstr "线路上的 CONNECT"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"HTTP CONNECT is useful as the next comparison point after SOCKS5 because it "
"solves nearly the same TCP-tunneling problem with a very different control "
"encoding. SOCKS5 uses compact binary fields; HTTP/1.1 CONNECT uses an HTTP "
"request and status response."
msgstr ""
"HTTP CONNECT 很适合作为 SOCKS5 之后的第二个比较基准：它解决几乎相同的 TCP 隧"
"道问题，但控制编码完全不同。SOCKS5 使用紧凑二进制字段，而 HTTP/1.1 CONNECT 使"
"用 HTTP 请求和状态响应。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP/1.1 request"
msgstr "HTTP/1.1 请求"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "A minimal request is:"
msgstr "最小请求如下："

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"The request target is the destination authority: `host:port`. RFC 9110 "
"requires an explicit port; CONNECT has no implicit default port. Unlike a "
"SOCKS5 request, there is no `ATYP` byte. The host is represented textually "
"and the HTTP parser separates the host and port according to CONNECT's "
"authority-form semantics."
msgstr ""
"请求目标是目标 authority：`host:port`。RFC 9110 要求显式提供端口，CONNECT 没"
"有隐含默认端口。与 SOCKS5 不同，它没有 `ATYP` 字节；主机以文本表示，由 HTTP "
"解析器按照 CONNECT 的 authority-form 语义拆分主机与端口。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"At the byte level the HTTP/1.1 control phase is therefore variable length:"
msgstr "因此在字节层面，HTTP/1.1 控制阶段是变长的："

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"The empty line terminates the HTTP header section. Bytes after the "
"successful CONNECT response are no longer ordinary HTTP/1.1 proxy-control "
"messages; they belong to the tunneled protocol."
msgstr ""
"空行用于结束 HTTP 头部。成功 CONNECT 响应之后的字节不再属于普通 HTTP/1.1 代理"
"控制消息，而属于被隧道承载的协议。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "Successful response and protocol switch"
msgstr "成功响应与协议切换"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "A proxy normally replies with a response such as:"
msgstr "代理通常返回类似以下响应："

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"RFC 9110 defines **any 2xx response** to CONNECT as success. Immediately "
"after the response header section, both sides switch to tunnel mode. A "
"successful CONNECT response must not define a message body with `Content-"
"Length` or `Transfer-Encoding`; clients ignore those fields if a non-"
"conforming proxy sends them."
msgstr ""
"RFC 9110 将 CONNECT 的**任意 2xx 响应**定义为成功。响应头结束后，双方立即切换"
"到隧道模式。成功 CONNECT 响应不能通过 `Content-Length` 或 `Transfer-"
"Encoding` 定义消息体；如果不合规代理发送这些字段，客户端应忽略。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "This creates a sharp state boundary:"
msgstr "这形成了一个非常明确的状态边界："

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"For HTTPS, the first bytes after the 2xx response are normally a TLS "
"`ClientHello` from the application. The proxy does not need to understand "
"that TLS handshake when it is operating as a blind tunnel."
msgstr ""
"对于 HTTPS，2xx 响应后的第一批字节通常是应用发送的 TLS `ClientHello`。代理作"
"为盲隧道工作时，并不需要理解这次 TLS 握手。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "Proxy authentication exchange"
msgstr "代理认证交互"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"Proxy authentication is not a fixed pre-request negotiation like SOCKS5 "
"method selection. An HTTP proxy can challenge a request with `407 Proxy "
"Authentication Required` and at least one `Proxy-Authenticate` challenge. "
"The client can then repeat CONNECT with `Proxy-Authorization` credentials."
msgstr ""
"代理认证不像 SOCKS5 METHOD 选择那样是固定的请求前协商。HTTP 代理可以通过 "
"`407 Proxy Authentication Required` 和至少一个 `Proxy-Authenticate` "
"challenge 拒绝请求，客户端随后携带 `Proxy-Authorization` 凭据重新发送 "
"CONNECT。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"Client -> Proxy\n"
"CONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1\n"
"\n"
"Proxy -> Client\n"
"HTTP/1.1 407 Proxy Authentication Required\n"
"Proxy-Authenticate: Basic realm=\"proxy\"\n"
"\n"
"Client -> Proxy\n"
"CONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1\n"
"Proxy-Authorization: Basic <credentials>\n"
"\n"
"Proxy -> Client\n"
"HTTP/1.1 200 Connection Established\n"
"\n"
"Client <=============================> Destination\n"
"              opaque tunnel bytes\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"客户端 -> 代理\n"
"CONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1\n"
"\n"
"代理 -> 客户端\n"
"HTTP/1.1 407 Proxy Authentication Required\n"
"Proxy-Authenticate: Basic realm=\"proxy\"\n"
"\n"
"客户端 -> 代理\n"
"CONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1\n"
"Proxy-Authorization: Basic <credentials>\n"
"\n"
"代理 -> 客户端\n"
"HTTP/1.1 200 Connection Established\n"
"\n"
"客户端 <=============================> 目标\n"
"                 透明隧道字节\n"
"```"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"The exact credential bytes depend on the selected HTTP authentication "
"scheme. Basic authentication, for example, is not encryption and should not "
"be exposed on an untrusted clear-text proxy connection."
msgstr ""
"具体凭据字节取决于选定的 HTTP 认证方案。例如 Basic Authentication 并不是加"
"密，不应通过不可信的明文代理连接暴露。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP/2 CONNECT: one tunnel per HTTP/2 stream"
msgstr "HTTP/2 CONNECT：每个 HTTP/2 Stream 承载一条隧道"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"CONNECT is an HTTP semantic, not an HTTP/1.1 text-format feature. HTTP/2 "
"keeps the proxy connection as an ordinary multiplexed HTTP/2 connection and "
"converts only the request stream into a tunnel. This is a fundamental "
"difference from HTTP/1.1 CONNECT, where the entire client-to-proxy TCP "
"connection changes into tunnel mode."
msgstr ""
"CONNECT 是 HTTP 语义，而不是 HTTP/1.1 文本格式独有的特性。HTTP/2 会让代理连接"
"继续保持为普通的多路复用 HTTP/2 连接，只把对应的请求 Stream 转换为隧道。这与 "
"HTTP/1.1 CONNECT 有根本区别：后者会把客户端到代理之间的整条 TCP 连接切换为隧"
"道模式。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "The request header section has these required pseudo-header semantics:"
msgstr "请求头部段必须遵循以下伪头字段语义："

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"The header block is HPACK-compressed inside a `HEADERS` frame, so those "
"strings are semantic fields rather than a fixed byte prefix. A simplified "
"HTTP/2 frame header is:"
msgstr ""
"头部块会经过 HPACK 压缩并放入 `HEADERS` 帧，因此这些字符串是语义字段，而不是"
"固定字节前缀。简化后的 HTTP/2 帧头如下："

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"For the CONNECT request, `Type=0x01` denotes `HEADERS`. On success, the "
"proxy returns response `HEADERS` carrying a `:status` in the 2xx range. "
"After the initial request and response header sections, tunnel octets are "
"carried in HTTP/2 `DATA` frames (`Type=0x00`) on that same stream:"
msgstr ""
"对 CONNECT 请求而言，`Type=0x01` 表示 `HEADERS`。成功时，代理返回携带 2xx "
"`:status` 的响应 `HEADERS`。初始请求和响应头部段结束后，隧道字节由同一 "
"Stream 上的 HTTP/2 `DATA` 帧（`Type=0x00`）承载："

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"Multiple CONNECT tunnels can therefore coexist on one HTTP/2 connection. "
"Their `DATA` frames can be interleaved, but the Stream Identifier keeps "
"tunnel bytes separate. This multiplexing is an extra transport layer that "
"standard SOCKS5 does not define."
msgstr ""
"因此，一条 HTTP/2 连接上可以同时存在多条 CONNECT 隧道。不同隧道的 `DATA` 帧可"
"以交错发送，但 Stream Identifier 会保持各隧道字节彼此隔离。这种多路复用属于标"
"准 SOCKS5 未定义的额外传输层能力。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"HTTP/2 `DATA` is subject to both connection-level and stream-level HTTP/2 "
"flow control. A CONNECT tunnel can therefore stop making progress even when "
"its upstream TCP socket is writable if the peer has not supplied enough "
"`WINDOW_UPDATE` credit. Conversely, one blocked stream does not require the "
"other CONNECT streams to stop, provided connection-level credit remains."
msgstr ""
"HTTP/2 `DATA` 同时受连接级和 Stream 级 HTTP/2 流控约束。因此，即使上游 TCP "
"socket 仍可写，只要对端没有提供足够的 `WINDOW_UPDATE` 额度，某条 CONNECT 隧道"
"也可能停止推进。反过来，只要连接级额度仍然充足，一条被阻塞的 Stream 并不要求"
"其他 CONNECT Stream 一起停止。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"After CONNECT succeeds, ordinary tunnel bytes are not additional HTTP "
"messages. RFC 9113 permits `DATA` plus stream-management frames on the "
"connected stream; a protocol implementation must not try to parse a TLS "
"`ClientHello` inside a `DATA` payload as another HTTP request."
msgstr ""
"CONNECT 成功后，普通隧道字节不再是新的 HTTP 消息。RFC 9113 允许已建立隧道的 "
"Stream 上出现 `DATA` 和 Stream 管理帧；协议实现不能把 `DATA` payload 中的 "
"TLS `ClientHello` 再当成另一个 HTTP 请求解析。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP/2 half-close and reset mapping"
msgstr "HTTP/2 半关闭与 Reset 映射"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"HTTP/2 maps the lifetime of the tunneled TCP connection onto the CONNECT "
"stream:"
msgstr "HTTP/2 会把被隧道化 TCP 连接的生命周期映射到 CONNECT Stream："

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"`END_STREAM` in the client-to-proxy direction corresponds to TCP FIN toward "
"the destination after any accompanying DATA bytes are forwarded;"
msgstr ""
"客户端到代理方向的 `END_STREAM` 表示：先转发随帧携带的 DATA 字节，再向目标连"
"接发送 TCP FIN；"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"a destination TCP FIN causes the proxy to finish its sending direction with "
"`END_STREAM`;"
msgstr ""
"目标端发送 TCP FIN 时，代理会以 `END_STREAM` 结束自身向客户端的发送方向；"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"a TCP reset or other TCP connection error is represented as `RST_STREAM` "
"with `CONNECT_ERROR`;"
msgstr ""
"TCP Reset 或其他 TCP 连接错误会表示为带 `CONNECT_ERROR` 的 `RST_STREAM`；"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"a stream error detected by the proxy requires the corresponding target TCP "
"connection to be aborted rather than silently reused."
msgstr ""
"代理检测到 Stream 错误时，需要中止对应的目标 TCP 连接，而不能静默复用该连接。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"This is more precise than saying that a tunnel simply \"closes\" when one "
"side finishes. HTTP/2, like TCP, can represent a half-closed direction, and "
"the other direction can still contain bytes that need to drain."
msgstr ""
"这比简单地说“一侧结束后隧道就关闭”更准确。HTTP/2 与 TCP 一样可以表示单方向半"
"关闭，而另一个方向仍可能存在需要继续排空的字节。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP/3 CONNECT: the same semantics over a QUIC request stream"
msgstr "HTTP/3 CONNECT：在 QUIC 请求 Stream 上承载相同语义"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"HTTP/3 retains the same CONNECT pseudo-header rules but maps each request "
"onto a client-initiated bidirectional QUIC stream. The request begins with "
"HTTP/3 `HEADERS`, the proxy responds with `HEADERS` containing a 2xx "
"`:status`, and subsequent HTTP/3 `DATA` frames on that request stream carry "
"the TCP tunnel. The request stream deliberately remains open after the "
"request header section."
msgstr ""
"HTTP/3 保留相同的 CONNECT 伪头字段规则，但会把每个请求映射到客户端发起的双向 "
"QUIC Stream。请求以 HTTP/3 `HEADERS` 开始，代理用包含 2xx `:status` 的 "
"`HEADERS` 响应，随后该请求 Stream 上的 HTTP/3 `DATA` 帧用于承载 TCP 隧道。请"
"求头部段结束后，这条请求 Stream 会有意保持打开。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"At the HTTP/3 framing layer, both frame type and frame length are QUIC "
"variable-length integers:"
msgstr "在 HTTP/3 分帧层，帧类型和帧长度都使用 QUIC 可变长度整数："

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"The HTTP/3 `HEADERS` payload is QPACK-encoded, so a passive capture cannot "
"treat `:method=CONNECT` or `:authority` as literal wire strings. After the "
"CONNECT exchange completes, ordinary tunnel octets reside in HTTP/3 DATA "
"payloads, and those HTTP/3 frames themselves are carried as QUIC STREAM "
"data. TCP segment boundaries at the target, HTTP/3 DATA frame boundaries, "
"QUIC STREAM frame boundaries, and UDP packet boundaries are all independent."
msgstr ""
"HTTP/3 `HEADERS` payload 使用 QPACK 编码，因此被动抓包不能把 "
"`:method=CONNECT` 或 `:authority` 当成线路上的明文字面字符串。CONNECT 交换完"
"成后，普通隧道字节位于 HTTP/3 DATA payload 中，而这些 HTTP/3 帧本身又作为 "
"QUIC STREAM 数据承载。目标侧 TCP segment 边界、HTTP/3 DATA 帧边界、QUIC "
"STREAM 帧边界以及 UDP 数据包边界彼此独立。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"HTTP/3 closes a normal tunnel direction using QUIC stream completion. If the "
"client finishes its sending direction, the proxy maps that completion to a "
"TCP FIN toward the target. A TCP reset or abnormal target close is "
"represented as a stream error with `H3_CONNECT_ERROR (0x010f)`. Resetting or "
"aborting one request stream does not inherently close unrelated CONNECT "
"streams, but a QUIC connection-level failure destroys every tunnel "
"multiplexed on that connection."
msgstr ""
"HTTP/3 通过 QUIC Stream 的方向完成来关闭普通隧道的一个方向。客户端结束发送方"
"向时，代理会把该完成状态映射为发往目标端的 TCP FIN。TCP Reset 或目标异常关闭"
"会表示为 `H3_CONNECT_ERROR (0x010f)` Stream 错误。Reset 或中止一条请求 "
"Stream 本身不会关闭无关的 CONNECT Stream，但 QUIC 连接级故障会终止复用在该连"
"接上的所有隧道。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"HTTP/3 flow control is provided by QUIC rather than HTTP/2 `WINDOW_UPDATE` "
"frames. The CONNECT request stream consumes QUIC stream and connection flow-"
"control credit, and all CONNECT streams on the connection also share the "
"QUIC congestion controller and path capacity. Thus \"many tunnels on one "
"connection\" does not mean each tunnel has independent physical bandwidth."
msgstr ""
"HTTP/3 的流控由 QUIC 提供，而不是使用 HTTP/2 `WINDOW_UPDATE` 帧。CONNECT 请"
"求 Stream 会消耗 QUIC Stream 级与连接级流控额度，并且同一连接上的所有 "
"CONNECT Stream 还共享 QUIC 拥塞控制器和链路容量。因此，“一条连接上有很多隧道”"
"并不意味着每条隧道都有独立的物理带宽。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "Ordinary CONNECT versus Extended CONNECT"
msgstr "普通 CONNECT 与 Extended CONNECT"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"Do not confuse basic proxy CONNECT with **Extended CONNECT**. RFC 8441 adds "
"the `:protocol` pseudo-header after explicit capability negotiation for uses "
"such as bootstrapping WebSocket over HTTP/2. Extended CONNECT changes the "
"request shape: it can include `:protocol` and, in that mode, `:scheme` and "
"`:path` are present. A normal forward proxy tunnel to `example.com:443` uses "
"the ordinary CONNECT form described above and does not need `:protocol`."
msgstr ""
"不要把基础代理 CONNECT 与 **Extended CONNECT** 混淆。RFC 8441 在显式能力协商"
"之后加入 `:protocol` 伪头字段，可用于在 HTTP/2 上引导 WebSocket 等协议。"
"Extended CONNECT 会改变请求形态：它可以包含 `:protocol`，并且在该模式下会同时"
"出现 `:scheme` 和 `:path`。普通正向代理到 `example.com:443` 的隧道使用前述普"
"通 CONNECT 形式，不需要 `:protocol`。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"This distinction is particularly useful when reading captures or XHTTP-"
"related documentation: seeing CONNECT on an HTTP/2 or HTTP/3 stream does not "
"by itself mean that the stream is a classic forward-proxy TCP tunnel."
msgstr ""
"在阅读抓包或 XHTTP 相关文档时，这一区分尤其重要：在 HTTP/2 或 HTTP/3 Stream "
"上看到 CONNECT，并不自动意味着该 Stream 就是经典正向代理 TCP 隧道。"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "Version-specific packet-capture anchors"
msgstr "各 HTTP 版本的抓包锚点"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid "The useful capture anchors differ by HTTP version:"
msgstr "不同 HTTP 版本可用的抓包锚点并不相同："

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"HTTP/1.1 clear text\n"
"  TCP -> \"CONNECT host:port HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\" -> 2xx -> opaque tunnel bytes\n"
"\n"
"HTTP/2\n"
"  TCP/TLS -> HTTP/2 stream N\n"
"             HEADERS(:method CONNECT, :authority ...)\n"
"             HEADERS(:status 2xx)\n"
"             DATA / DATA / ... / END_STREAM or RST_STREAM\n"
"\n"
"HTTP/3\n"
"  UDP -> QUIC -> request stream N\n"
"                HEADERS(:method CONNECT, :authority ...)\n"
"                HEADERS(:status 2xx)\n"
"                DATA / DATA / ... / QUIC FIN or stream reset\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"HTTP/1.1 明文\n"
"  TCP -> \"CONNECT host:port HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\" -> 2xx -> 不透明隧道字节\n"
"\n"
"HTTP/2\n"
"  TCP/TLS -> HTTP/2 stream N\n"
"             HEADERS(:method CONNECT, :authority ...)\n"
"             HEADERS(:status 2xx)\n"
"             DATA / DATA / ... / END_STREAM 或 RST_STREAM\n"
"\n"
"HTTP/3\n"
"  UDP -> QUIC -> request stream N\n"
"                HEADERS(:method CONNECT, :authority ...)\n"
"                HEADERS(:status 2xx)\n"
"                DATA / DATA / ... / QUIC FIN 或 stream reset\n"
"```"

#: src/protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"Without the TLS/QUIC decryption material, encrypted HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 "
"captures usually expose transport behavior rather than the target authority "
"or tunnel contents. With decryption, a dissector should follow the request "
"stream and its header compression context instead of searching raw packets "
"for the ASCII word `CONNECT`."
msgstr ""
"如果没有 TLS/QUIC 解密材料，加密 HTTP/2 与 HTTP/3 抓包通常只能暴露传输行为，"
"而看不到目标 authority 或隧道内容。完成解密后，协议分析器应跟踪对应请求 "
"Stream 及其头部压缩上下文，而不是在原始数据包里搜索 ASCII 字符串 `CONNECT`。"

