"XHTTP is an Xray transport method used to carry proxy traffic through HTTP-"
"shaped request/response flows. It belongs to the transport layer, not the "
"proxy-protocol layer. This page owns HTTP framing, session handling, and "
"transport settings; proxy identity/destination rules belong to the [Proxy "
"Protocol Reference](../protocol.md), and TLS/REALITY settings belong to "
"[Transport Security](../transport-security.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/transports/xhttp.md
msgid "A typical deployment combines:"
